    <string name="what_is_wif">WHAT IS WIF?</string>
    <string name="wif_short_explanation">WIF is the Wallet Import Format for a Bitcoin private key. It is sensitive: anyone who has it can spend the funds controlled by that key.</string>
    <string name="wif_info_message">WIF (Wallet Import Format) is a text representation of a Bitcoin private key.\n
\n
Use it when you intentionally need to import an existing private key into this main wallet. Paste the WIF into the field above, then choose IMPORT PRIVATE KEY. The wallet converts it to the private key and stores it in the wallet.\n
\n
A WIF is not a receiving address and it is not a recovery phrase. It is secret spending authority for one private key.\n
\n
Never send a WIF to anyone, put it in screenshots, chat messages, cloud notes, or logs. Anyone who obtains it may be able to spend the Bitcoin controlled by that key. Only use WIF import when you know exactly where the private key came from and why it needs to be imported.</string>
